      "basis": "Replace the two mapped church/monastery shells, with2cm numeric pad, subtracting all independent neighboring footprints plus1mm protection. Original map controls overlap Town Hall/cafe edges slightly: protected residual control fragments stay entirely inside those independent footprint envelopes. Preserve all independent inputs and native ground/water."
    },
    "notes": "Named standard PMTiles church building/POI35184576280912 and monastery building/POI52776561095808, correlated with ordinary facade/cloister pictures, establish the two authored controls. Named monastery point corresponds to mapped relation2962560; no exact-QID footprint attribution claimed. Anchor-8.428761,40.210945; heading0, internal local+x angle-.154600686944rad, west entrance local-x. The mapped courtyard hole is retained. Town Hall35184576280911 and Cafe Santa Cruz35184595417581 remain independent native buildings. Original standard6m Mapzen ground/water and all independent buildings retained. Each mapped structure has a small grade-buried local plinth; cloister courts stay native ground, entrance has short descending steps. No broad monastery/plaza slab, flattening or ground/water cutout. Coarse urban DEM does not resolve actual paved court/plaza floors or thresholds; absolute heights and approaches remain approximate."
  },
  "scaleBasis": "Ordinary-picture/map visualization estimates, not surveyed dimensions: approximately38.9m church length/18.5m west-front width, nave19m eaves/22m tile ridge, western stone screen24.2m, tower pinnacles29m/cross30m, center cross29m. Cloister lower arcade5m, upper glazed arcade/eaves9m, higher white outer ranges12m/terracotta ridges14m. Specific sculpture, bay subdivisions, concealed roofs and exact floor/stair levels remain approximate.",
